{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1489779211,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4NzQ1MDc3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1384#issuecomment-287450776"},"message":"bloody setuptools!  I found no reliable way to \"override\" its behavior regarding installation of the scripts.  Mere import of the setuptools is sufficient to \"augment\" distutils behavior and lead to creation of those \"script runners\" even on linux:\n\n1. simple setuputils scripts spec - already creates its shim\n```shell\n$\u003e deactivate; rm -rf /tmp/testproj; mkdir /tmp/testproj; cd /tmp/testproj; echo -e 'from setuptools import setup;\\nsetup(scripts=[\"script1\"])' \u003e setup.py; echo -e '#!/usr/bin/env python\\nprint(\"#RUN\")' \u003e script1; virtualenv venv; source venv/bin/activate; python setup.py install \u003e/dev/null; which script1 | xargs cat ; \nRunning virtualenv with interpreter /usr/bin/python2\nNew python executable in /tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python2\nAlso creating executable in /tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python\nInstalling setuptools, pkg_resources, pip, wheel...done.\nwarning: install_lib: 'build/lib.linux-x86_64-2.7' does not exist -- no Python modules to install\n\nzip_safe flag not set; analyzing archive contents...\n#!/tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python\n# EASY-INSTALL-SCRIPT: 'UNKNOWN==0.0.0','script1'\n__requires__ = 'UNKNOWN==0.0.0'\n__import__('pkg_resources').run_script('UNKNOWN==0.0.0', 'script1')\n```\n2. with distuils it is all nice and dandy:\n```shell\n$\u003e deactivate; rm -rf /tmp/testproj; mkdir /tmp/testproj; cd /tmp/testproj; echo -e 'from distutils.core import setup;\\nsetup(scripts=[\"script1\"])' \u003e setup.py; echo -e '#!/usr/bin/env python\\nprint(\"#RUN\")' \u003e script1; virtualenv venv; source venv/bin/activate; python setup.py install \u003e/dev/null; which script1 | xargs cat ;          \nRunning virtualenv with interpreter /usr/bin/python2\nNew python executable in /tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python2\nAlso creating executable in /tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python\nInstalling setuptools, pkg_resources, pip, wheel...done.\n#!/tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python\nprint(\"#RUN\")\n```\n3. and then if we just import setuptools after distutils:\n```shell\n$\u003e deactivate; rm -rf /tmp/testproj; mkdir /tmp/testproj; cd /tmp/testproj; echo -e 'from distutils.core import setup;\\nimport setuptools; setup(scripts=[\"script1\"])' \u003e setup.py; echo -e '#!/usr/bin/env python\\nprint(\"#RUN\")' \u003e script1; virtualenv venv; source venv/bin/activate; python setup.py install \u003e/dev/null; which script1 | xargs cat ;                    \nRunning virtualenv with interpreter /usr/bin/python2\nNew python executable in /tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python2\nAlso creating executable in /tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python\nInstalling setuptools, pkg_resources, pip, wheel...done.\nwarning: install_lib: 'build/lib.linux-x86_64-2.7' does not exist -- no Python modules to install\n\nzip_safe flag not set; analyzing archive contents...\n#!/tmp/testproj/venv/bin/python\n# EASY-INSTALL-SCRIPT: 'UNKNOWN==0.0.0','script1'\n__requires__ = 'UNKNOWN==0.0.0'\n__import__('pkg_resources').run_script('UNKNOWN==0.0.0', 'script1')\n```\nbleh... btw -- executing this one takes already 100ms! (plain script is just around 3ms)","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1489905144,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTAwNTc2MDY2NA=="},"status":2}]}